\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O what shall I do my Saviour to praise,
\par So faithful and true, so plenteous in grace,
\par So strong to deliver, so good to redeem
\par The weakest believer that hangs upon Him.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. How happy the man whose heart is set free,
\par The people that can be joyful in Thee;
\par Their joy is to walk in the light of Thy face,
\par And still they are  talking of Jesus's grace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Their daily delight shall be in Thy name;
\par They shall as their right Thy righteousness claim;
\par Thy righteousness wearing, and cleansed by Thy blood,
\par Bold shall they appear in the presence of God.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. For Jesus, my Lord, is now my defence;
\par I trust in His word, none plucks me from thence,
\par Since I have found favour, He all things will do;
\par My King and my Saviour shall make me anew.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

